{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01065",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.17,
      "end_seconds": 6.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "Doctor, if you're free, we can start. I've got the numbers noted down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.12,
      "end_seconds": 12.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Okay, good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.59,
      "end_seconds": 19.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "Doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.39,
      "end_seconds": 25.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.94,
      "end_seconds": 39.44,
      "duration_seconds": 12.5,
      "text": "Actually, uh, so the thing is, I've got yellow eyes. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.29,
      "end_seconds": 42.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.9,
      "end_seconds": 49.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Uh, I'd say about a month, maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 50.55,
      "end_seconds": 55.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "I think it's been nearer about two months, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.81,
      "end_seconds": 60.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.07,
      "end_seconds": 63.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "That sounds about right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.77,
      "end_seconds": 70.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "And, And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 70.89,
      "end_seconds": 76.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "Yeah, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.32,
      "end_seconds": 80.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.25,
      "end_seconds": 90.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything. Have you had dark urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.4,
      "end_seconds": 99.52,
      "duration_seconds": 8.12,
      "text": "Yeah, um, that too. Oh, and no appetite. That's been about the same, about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 100.95,
      "end_seconds": 112.15,
      "duration_seconds": 11.2,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pressure 110 over 77, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, pulse is 79 beats a minute, temperature is 36.7 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.09,
      "end_seconds": 117.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.59,
      "end_seconds": 121.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.19,
      "end_seconds": 123.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.21,
      "end_seconds": 126.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.86,
      "end_seconds": 143.05,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "The whites of your eyes are yellow and the liver edge is tender under the right ribs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.81,
      "end_seconds": 153.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. A few quick ones: fever, itching or bleeding?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.46,
      "end_seconds": 167.2,
      "duration_seconds": 11.74,
      "text": "Yeah, no, no fever, no itching, no bleeding. I did have tiredness at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.01,
      "end_seconds": 168.84,
      "duration_seconds": 0.83,
      "text": "Any confusion?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.59,
      "end_seconds": 172.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any confusion."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.85,
      "end_seconds": 178.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "A few quick ones: vomiting blood or severe abdominal pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.22,
      "end_seconds": 185.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Actually, no, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.52,
      "end_seconds": 188.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Right, neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.06,
      "end_seconds": 193.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.19,
      "end_seconds": 196.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.48,
      "end_seconds": 201.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.99,
      "end_seconds": 204.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.53,
      "end_seconds": 213.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.84,
      "end_seconds": 224.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 226.62,
      "end_seconds": 236.58,
      "duration_seconds": 9.96,
      "text": "Well, she takes febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day for the gout. She takes hydrocortisone cream, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.29,
      "end_seconds": 241.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.98,
      "end_seconds": 247.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Hmm, I don't think I have any, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 247.87,
      "end_seconds": 253.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "I'm not sure that's right. I seem to recall a problem with tramadol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.86,
      "end_seconds": 257.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Maybe, but I don't recall it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.28,
      "end_seconds": 264.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.79,
      "end_seconds": 284.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Okay, anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.54,
      "end_seconds": 288.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "I have gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.03,
      "end_seconds": 290.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.6,
      "end_seconds": 295.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Actually, I've had eczema for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.28,
      "end_seconds": 297.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.99,
      "end_seconds": 301.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "No, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.09,
      "end_seconds": 305.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.54,
      "end_seconds": 311.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "My aunt has rheumatoid arthritis. My uncle has high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.88,
      "end_seconds": 328.35,
      "duration_seconds": 15.47,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. I'm honestly not certain yet. It could be an acute viral hepatitis, or it might be a drug-related liver problem. We shouldn't forget gallstones blocking the bile duct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.28,
      "end_seconds": 332.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.16,
      "end_seconds": 349.01,
      "duration_seconds": 15.85,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an acute viral hepatitis, but I'd like to confirm. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had yellow eyes, and no severe abdominal pain or itching."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.79,
      "end_seconds": 351.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.42,
      "end_seconds": 370.22,
      "duration_seconds": 16.8,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange liver blood tests for jaundice. I think an ultrasound of the liver makes sense here, for jaundice. No alcohol at all and avoid paracetamol and other painkillers unless we say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.9,
      "end_seconds": 376.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "Mm, do I need a hepatitis screen? I read it might help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.27,
      "end_seconds": 387.5,
      "duration_seconds": 9.23,
      "text": "I wouldn't order it today. If anything changes, we'll reconsider. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.15,
      "end_seconds": 390.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.09,
      "end_seconds": 393.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}